<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gatun Lake</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gatun Lake is an artificial lake in Panama formed by the Gatun Dam on the Chagres River, built between 1907 and 1913, and on completion the largest man-made lake in the world. It forms a major part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal">Panama Canal</a> route, carrying ships 26 metres above sea level between the locks, and supplies the water used in each lock operation. Droughts, notably in 2023–2024, have forced restrictions on canal traffic.</p></div>
